# debian/source/lintian-overrides
#
# A "lintian override" tells the lintian QA tool: "I know about this warning,
# it is expected, stop reporting it." Each non-comment line below is the exact
# text of a lintian tag we are silencing, plus the reason.
#
# Why we need it:
#   The debhelper "dkms" helper (dh_dkms) used to live inside the "dkms"
#   package. From Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) / Debian 13 it was split into a separate
#   "dh-dkms" package, and on 24.04 the old "dkms" package no longer provides
#   that helper. But Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) has NO "dh-dkms" package at all.
#
#   To build on BOTH releases from one control file we must write
#   "dh-dkms | dkms" (try dh-dkms first, fall back to dkms). lintian cannot
#   prove the helper is available via the "dkms" fallback, so it complains.
#   The complaint is harmless here, so we override it.
limesuiteng source: missing-build-dependency-for-dh-addon dkms (does not satisfy dh-dkms:any) [debian/rules]
limesuiteng source: missing-build-dependency-for-dh_-command dh_dkms (does not satisfy dh-dkms:any | dh-sequence-dkms:any) [debian/rules]
